WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.632
Module 6: your practical.

00:00:01.632 --> 00:00:04.373
Northwind ran the study you helped design,

00:00:04.373 --> 00:00:08.942
and two hundred and four stories came
in between January and February.

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:13.968
Alex Moreau wants to know what they say
before the decision-rights charter is

00:00:13.968 --> 00:00:14.686
redesigned.

00:00:14.686 --> 00:00:18.863
Your job is to find the patterns
and the stories that don't fit,

00:00:18.863 --> 00:00:23.432
be honest about what the data can't
tell, and recommend the next wave.

00:00:23.933 --> 00:00:26.068
You've passed the module checks.

00:00:26.068 --> 00:00:27.269
Two things remain.

00:00:27.269 --> 00:00:31.872
The final exam has thirty questions,
takes about thirty-five minutes,

00:00:31.872 --> 00:00:33.073
and is open notes.

00:00:33.073 --> 00:00:38.610
You need eighty percent, and every one of
the three questions on unbreakable rules.

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:40.811
Passing it completes this course.

00:00:40.811 --> 00:00:44.881
Your memo is task three of your
Mosaic Practitioner capstone.

00:00:44.881 --> 00:00:50.017
It's up to two pages, and every rubric
criterion needs a three out of four or

00:00:50.017 --> 00:00:50.484
better.

00:00:50.484 --> 00:00:53.086
You get one resubmission with feedback.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:54.905
Here's Alex's brief.

00:00:54.905 --> 00:00:57.059
Before the charter is redesigned,

00:00:57.059 --> 00:01:02.345
they need to know what the stories say
about how decisions land on the frontline,

00:01:02.345 --> 00:01:06.522
how solid that is, and what
Northwind should run next, and when,

00:01:06.522 --> 00:01:09.590
to see whether the redesign
makes a difference.

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:14.158
You can draw on the Culture Mosaic
and the October progress check too.

00:01:14.667 --> 00:01:16.117
This is your dataset.

00:01:16.117 --> 00:01:19.293
It has the triad on what
shaped each decision,

00:01:19.293 --> 00:01:24.609
the two sliders on when people heard
and what they did next, the four stones,

00:01:24.609 --> 00:01:28.613
the context counts, and ten
stories with their placements.

00:01:28.613 --> 00:01:32.342
Every number is also in
section five of the case file.

00:01:32.342 --> 00:01:38.072
Read the shapes before the averages, slice
carefully, and check every group's size.

00:01:38.567 --> 00:01:41.768
Write a memo to Alex of
no more than two pages.

00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:43.880
Include three to five patterns,

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:49.126
each with a count of stories out of the
total and a paraphrased story or two.

00:01:49.126 --> 00:01:52.804
Name two or three outlier
stories and why they matter.

00:01:52.804 --> 00:01:54.235
Set out the cautions.

00:01:54.235 --> 00:01:55.870
Recommend the next wave.

00:01:55.870 --> 00:01:59.549
And add a short note on what
you will and won't share.

00:01:59.549 --> 00:02:02.887
Paraphrase every story
and keep small groups out.

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:09.060
The assessor scores six criteria:
reading the shapes, evidence and stories,

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:13.287
outlier stories, confidence
and cautions, the next wave,

00:02:13.287 --> 00:02:15.627
and ethics and confidentiality.

00:02:15.627 --> 00:02:21.211
Each is scored one to four, and you
need a three or better on all of them.

00:02:21.211 --> 00:02:26.645
Three things fail a memo outright:
presenting a group under ten stories,

00:02:26.645 --> 00:02:32.683
trying to identify a storyteller, or
presenting a score, a benchmark or a cause.

00:02:33.167 --> 00:02:36.050
When you're ready, start the final exam.

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:38.141
Thirty questions, open notes.

00:02:38.141 --> 00:02:38.861
Good luck.

00:02:39.367 --> 00:02:42.138
Pass the exam and this course is complete.

00:02:42.138 --> 00:02:47.021
Once you've also finished the Mosaic
Practitioner and Culture Dig courses,

00:02:47.021 --> 00:02:50.255
hand in your memo with
the rest of your capstone.

00:02:50.255 --> 00:02:52.366
When all four tasks have passed,

00:02:52.366 --> 00:02:55.797
you're Mosaic Practitioner
Certified for five years.

00:02:55.797 --> 00:02:57.777
Keep your four job aids close.

00:02:57.777 --> 00:03:00.680
Your next study will
have its own surprises.

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:04.970
Read the shape before the average,
the stories before the claims,

00:03:04.970 --> 00:03:07.213
and treat every outlier as a clue.
